From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:52:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 002/159] [ae-patch] Add a server.request host method and ae.*
 labels on extension session summaries

Phase 3 of omnigent-ae (patch P2, 2026-09-23). The Parking Lot page is an
extension, so its only bridge to data is the host RPC; this patch gives that
RPC exactly what the page needs and nothing more.

`server.request` is a new host method behind a new `server.request`
permission. It is an allowlist over the host's authenticated fetch, not a
proxy: `GET` and `POST` under `/v1/ae/`, `PATCH /v1/sessions/{id}` whose
body is `labels` only with every key under `ae.`, and
`POST /v1/sessions/{id}/events` carrying one user message. Anything else
(DELETE anywhere, a rename or archive through the PATCH, a label outside
`ae.*`, an assistant message, a route outside the list) is refused before any
network call. The body is rebuilt from the allowlisted fields, both directions
are held to the RPC message budget, and a labels write invalidates the
`["conversations"]` cache so the sidebar follows. The server's own status and
JSON body come back as `{status, ok, body}` so the page reads upstream's
error shape itself.

Session summaries gain `labels`, filtered to `ae.*`, and `archived`. The
extension API version stays 1: both changes are additive and an older bundle
ignores the new fields.

Logic lives in new files (web/src/extensions/services/serverRequest.ts, the
`pickAeLabels` helper in web/src/lib/aeLabels.ts) so the upstream edits stay
small: one line in api.py, one in registry.ts, ten in
useExtensionHostServices.ts, three in sessions.ts, three in types.ts, and the
SDK's context type. Tests cover the allowlist (45 cases in
serverRequest.test.ts), the hook wiring and cache refresh, the projection,
and the SDK page drain.

